`src/sam_vtp_core/architecture.py` reproduces, in condensed form, the layer
definitions of SAM 2's Hiera image encoder, FPN neck, memory attention, memory
encoder and mask decoder, together with the memory read/write logic of
`SAM2Base`. Parameter names are preserved so that SAM 2 pretrained weights and
SAM-VTP checkpoints remain loadable.

Modifications relative to SAM 2:

  * The interactive prompt encoder is replaced by a fixed learned prompt
    (`LearnedPrompt`), since traversability has no user click.
  * Memory features are resampled into the current camera frame using depth and
    relative pose before memory attention (ego-motion warp).
  * Depth-derived geometry channels are added to the coarsest backbone level.
  * A full-resolution RGB-guided residual head refines the decoder's output.
  * Interactive-tracking paths not used by SAM-VTP (click refinement, reverse
    tracking, mask-as-output, non-overlap constraints, multi-object batching)
    are removed.
  * Hydra/OmegaConf configuration is replaced by a plain dataclass.

